    {
      "id": "demo.tiny-cpu",
      "name": "Tiny CPU",
      "description": "A 4-bit accumulator CPU with a 16-word instruction ROM and a 16x4 RAM. Opcodes: 0 NOP, 1 LDA #, 2 ADD #, 3 STA addr, 4 AND #, 5 OR #, 6 JMP, 7 JZ, 8 LDA@ addr, 9 ADD@ addr, 10 PUSH, 11 POP, 12 CALL addr, 13 RET. SP starts at 0 and points to the next free stack slot; PUSH/CALL increment it and POP/RET decrement it. CLR is synchronous with the next rising CLK edge; it clears PC, ACC, CARRY, and SP but leaves RAM contents intact. Instructions are opcode(4) | operand(4).",
